1) convert ligand pdb file to mol2 file using oenBABEL
2) change the name of file to ligand.mol2
3) log on  swissparam upload ligans.mol2 ....download ligand.zip. 
4) copy   ligand.pdb
		  ligand.itp
5)	Remove any ligand atoms from receptor protein

6)
/home/ngadewal/gromacs/gromacs-4.5.5-bin/bin/./pdb2gmx_d -f protein.pdb -ff charmm27 -water tip3p -ignh -o conf.pdb -nochargegrp

7) 
Modify the topol.top file generated by pdb2gmx. In the "Include chain topologies" section, add the following statement, before all other lines referring to the protein or ions :
  
; Include chain topologies
#include "ligand.itp"
  
(add above moleculetype] section.) 

8) Insert the ATOM lines from the ligand.pdb into the conf.pdb file, right after the line for the ion CAL. Atoms will be automatically renumbered in the next step.

